      body: "Darwin's Journey casts you as a young naturalist following Darwin across the Galápagos, and it is a rich, interlocking worker-placement euro underneath its handsome map. The clever hook is education: your workers must learn skills, level by level, before they can reach the most valuable spots on the board, so every placement is also an investment in future reach. From there you explore islands, dispatch correspondence, catalogue specimens and chase a tangle of contracts and end-game goals that reward tight, multi-turn planning. It is meaty and demands attention, plays cleanly from solo up to four, and layers just enough theme over a precise points engine. A satisfying pick for gamers ready to graduate to full-weight euros.",
