      body: "Forest Shuffle packs a surprising amount of game into a single deck of cards. You are building a forest, drafting animals, trees and plants from a shared display and layering them so each card tucks half-hidden beneath the next, forming symbiotic combos as your ecosystem grows. Trees anchor your tableau; the creatures and details you attach around them score in sharp, interlocking ways at the end. Every card is dual-use — currency or content — so the tension is constant and the deck-only footprint makes it a brilliant travel and café game. It teaches in minutes, plays in about an hour and hides real engine-building depth. A modern card-game gem that punches well above its box size.",
